1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,385
A Shortcut Through the Menu.

3
00:00:03,385 --> 00:00:05,885
Mom and I try a new sandwich shop.

4
00:00:05,885 --> 00:00:09,187
The menu has names like Garden Stack and Sunset Special.

5
00:00:09,187 --> 00:00:12,865
They sound beautiful, but I have no idea what I'm supposed to eat.

6
00:00:13,132 --> 00:00:14,501
You can ask.

7
00:00:14,501 --> 00:00:16,678
A name doesn't tell you everything.

8
00:00:16,948 --> 00:00:19,848
I point to the Garden Stack when the server comes over.

9
00:00:19,848 --> 00:00:21,535
What's in this sandwich?

10
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:26,328
Roasted vegetables, cheese, lettuce, and our house sauce, on toasted bread.

11
00:00:26,548 --> 00:00:28,258
Is the sauce spicy?

12
00:00:28,492 --> 00:00:29,652
A little.

13
00:00:29,652 --> 00:00:31,434
It has some chili in it.

14
00:00:31,434 --> 00:00:34,579
If you prefer, we can put it in a separate little cup.

15
00:00:34,852 --> 00:00:36,885
Could I have the sauce on the side?

16
00:00:37,108 --> 00:00:38,487
Absolutely.

17
00:00:38,487 --> 00:00:40,456
Anything else you'd like to know?

18
00:00:40,732 --> 00:00:42,403
No, thank you.

19
00:00:42,403 --> 00:00:43,924
That sounds good.

20
00:00:43,924 --> 00:00:47,726
Mom orders a different sandwich, and we sit by a shelf of plants.

21
00:00:47,726 --> 00:00:51,278
When our food arrives, I try a tiny bit of sauce first.

22
00:00:51,556 --> 00:00:52,881
How is it?

23
00:00:53,116 --> 00:00:55,339
Good, but a little is enough for me.

24
00:00:55,339 --> 00:00:59,162
I add some to one corner of the sandwich instead of pouring it over everything.

25
00:00:59,452 --> 00:01:00,984
Glad you asked?

26
00:01:01,204 --> 00:01:02,616
Very glad.

27
00:01:02,616 --> 00:01:06,458
I would have guessed Garden Stack meant a pile of lettuce with a flower on top.

28
00:01:06,748 --> 00:01:08,479
Everything okay here?

29
00:01:08,716 --> 00:01:10,397
Yes, thanks.

30
00:01:10,397 --> 00:01:12,366
Your garden is delicious.

31
00:01:12,366 --> 00:01:15,918
The server laughs, and Mom smiles over her sandwich.

32
00:01:15,918 --> 00:01:19,824
Next time a menu sounds like poetry, I'll ask about the ingredients.

33
00:01:19,824 --> 00:01:22,199
It's easier than trying to eat a sunset.
